# Environment variables

Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored — never commit it). Production values go in
Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

```bash
# ── Masumi hosted preprod ──────────────────────────────────────
MASUMI_PAYMENT_BASE_URL=https://<provided-by-organizers>/api/v1
MASUMI_PAYMENT_API_KEY=<read-and-pay key>
MASUMI_REGISTRY_BASE_URL=https://<provided-by-organizers>/api/v1
MASUMI_REGISTRY_API_KEY=<registry key>
MASUMI_NETWORK=Preprod
MASUMI_SELLING_WALLET_VKEY=<selling wallet vkey>

# ── ElevenLabs (CLI + voiceover; project-local, read from env) ──
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ── Models (OpenRouter, free-tier models; first in the list is primary) ─
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODELS=poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free,nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free,google/gemma-4-31b-it:free

# ── Demo flags ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# false = real Masumi preprod escrows; true = labelled simulated ledger
SIMULATE_PAYMENTS=false
# live = full run; canned = replay of a recorded successful run
DEMO_MODE=live

# ── Board state (Upstash Redis REST) ────────────────────────────
# Unset = in-memory store, fine for `npm run dev`, lost between serverless invocations.
# The Vercel Upstash integration injects KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN
# instead; the store reads either pair.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Outcome feed (demo-only signing key for the NeoRack signup feed) ─
# Generate locally: openssl rand -hex 32. Signs simulated signup events.
SHOP_SIGNING_KEY=

# ── Tender Board (demo-only signing key for Board-signed verdicts) ─
# Generate locally: openssl rand -hex 32. Ed25519 key is derived from it.
BOARD_SIGNING_KEY=
```

Rules: keys in Vercel env vars + `.env.local` only — never in the repo,
never in the browser, never on screen. Testnet tx hashes are public and
safe to commit.
